BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 780 Tm (RAGDoc: Retrieval-Augmented Question Answering over Scientific Documents) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 764 Tm () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 748 Tm (2. Related Work) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 732 Tm () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 716 Tm (Sparse retrieval with BM25 remains a strong baseline and is difficult to beat on queries) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 700 Tm (containing rare terms. Dense passage retrieval, introduced by Karpukhin et al., encodes queries) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 684 Tm (and passages into a shared vector space and substantially improves recall on paraphrased) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 668 Tm (queries. ColBERT proposes late interaction as a middle ground. Fusion methods including) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 652 Tm (Reciprocal Rank Fusion combine ranked lists without requiring score normalisation across) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 636 Tm (systems. A parallel line of work studies attribution directly. Early systems appended a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 620 Tm (bibliography of consulted sources without indicating which source supported which sentence, an) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 604 Tm (arrangement that offers the appearance of verifiability without its substance. Later work moves) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 588 Tm (to sentence-level attribution and reports that models frequently attach citations to claims the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 572 Tm (cited passage does not contain. Work on abstention is comparatively sparse. Calibration studies) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 556 Tm (show that model confidence correlates only loosely with correctness in open-ended generation,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 540 Tm (which suggests that thresholding on confidence is an unreliable route to declining gracefully.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 524 Tm (Approaches based on verifying candidate answers against retrieved evidence appear more robust,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 508 Tm (and our design follows that tradition. We differ principally in enforcing the constraint) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 492 Tm (structurally rather than statistically, so that an unsupported claim is prevented from being) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 476 Tm (emitted rather than detected after the fact.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 460 Tm () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 444 Tm (3) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
