BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 732 Tm () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 716 Tm (RAGDoc attains 84.2 F1 on our primary benchmark, compared with 77.8 F1 for the dense-only) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 700 Tm (baseline and 74.1 F1 for the lexical-only baseline. Attribution accuracy, measured as the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 684 Tm (proportion of generated claims traceable to a cited passage, reaches 91.6 percent. The system) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 668 Tm (abstains on 7.3 percent of questions, and manual inspection confirms that the overwhelming) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 652 Tm (majority of abstentions are cases the document genuinely does not address. The margin narrows) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 636 Tm (considerably on the internally constructed set, which we regard as the more informative) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 620 Tm (comparison for the reasons given in the preceding section. Both baselines degrade more sharply) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 604 Tm (than the full system when question and evidence share little vocabulary, and the ordering of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 588 Tm (the two baselines reverses on that slice. Latency is dominated by generation rather than) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 572 Tm (retrieval. Retrieval over a single document completes in a few tens of milliseconds and is not) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 556 Tm (the bottleneck at any document length we examined. Memory scales linearly in the number of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 540 Tm (passages, and a document of two hundred pages remains comfortably within the working set of a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 524 Tm (single commodity machine.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 508 Tm () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 492 Tm (9) Tj ET
