BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 764 Tm () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 748 Tm (9. Ablation Study) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 732 Tm () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 716 Tm (Removing the lexical ranker and retrieving with embeddings alone costs 3.1 F1, with the loss) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 700 Tm (concentrated on questions containing rare identifiers such as dataset names and equation) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 684 Tm (references. Removing the semantic ranker instead costs 5.7 F1, concentrated on paraphrased) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 668 Tm (questions sharing no vocabulary with the source passage. Reducing the number of retrieved) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 652 Tm (passages from five to two costs 4.2 F1. The asymmetry between the two ranker ablations is worth) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 636 Tm (dwelling on, because it is easy to misread. It does not establish that semantic matching is the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 620 Tm (more important mechanism in general. It reflects the composition of the evaluation set, in) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 604 Tm (which paraphrased questions outnumber those turning on a rare token. A corpus dense in) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 588 Tm (identifiers, model names, or numeric constants would shift the balance, and we observed exactly) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 572 Tm (that shift on the subset of our internal questions concerning experimental configuration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 556 Tm (Removing the distractor passages from training, while leaving the architecture unchanged, costs) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 540 Tm (2.4 F1 and degrades attribution accuracy considerably more than it degrades answer quality.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 524 Tm (This supports the view that attribution and answer quality are separable capabilities that) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 508 Tm (require separate supervision.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 492 Tm () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 476 Tm (10) Tj ET
