BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 732 Tm () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 716 Tm (We intend to add an optical character recognition stage so that scanned documents can be) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 700 Tm (processed. A second direction is multi-document retrieval, allowing a question to be answered) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 684 Tm (across a collection of related papers rather than a single one. We are also investigating query) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 668 Tm (rewriting so that conversational follow-up questions can be resolved against earlier turns in a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 652 Tm (dialogue. Sentence-level attribution is the most direct response to the granularity limitation) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 636 Tm (discussed above, and a promising route runs through a lightweight verification pass that aligns) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 620 Tm (each emitted claim against spans within its cited passage. Preliminary experiments suggest the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 604 Tm (additional latency is tolerable when the pass runs only over claims the generator has already) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 588 Tm (committed to. A more speculative direction concerns documents that disagree with one another.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 572 Tm (Once retrieval spans a collection, conflicting evidence becomes the normal case rather than an) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 556 Tm (anomaly, and presenting a single answer misrepresents the state of the literature. We consider) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 540 Tm (surfacing the disagreement to be the correct behaviour, though the interface question is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 524 Tm (unresolved.) Tj ET
